Requirements:
1. QEMU >= 8.2.10 because we use netduinoplus2 board.
   You may need to build from source because the QEMU installed with your Ubuntu may not be of the correct version.
   ref: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/79610213/does-qemu-virt-board-really-support-cortex-m4-processor
2.


Preparation Steps:
0. Install toolchain
   sudo apt install ninja-build libglib2.0-dev flex bison

1. Build latest QEMU from source (ref: https://github.com/qemu/qemu).
   The commit I am using is bb7fc1543f.
   You may need to install below dependencies.
   sudo apt install flex bison libglib2.0-dev libfdt-dev libpmem-dev libdaxctl-dev libcbor-dev libudev-dev libdw-dev libusb-dev librdmacm-dev libiscsi-dev libnfs-dev libssh-dev

   git clone git@github.com:qemu/qemu.git
   cd qemu
   mkdir build
   cd build
   ../configure
   make
   sudo make install

2. Download ARM toolchain
   Goto: https://developer.arm.com/downloads/-/arm-gnu-toolchain-downloads
   wget https://developer.arm.com/-/media/Files/downloads/gnu/14.3.rel1/binrel/arm-gnu-toolchain-14.3.rel1-x86_64-arm-none-eabi.tar.xz
   tar -vxf ./arm-gnu-toolchain-14.3.rel1-x86_64-arm-none-eabi.tar.xz
   Change the toolchain path in the Makefile.

3. Build
   Choose the mk file for a board and build. Such as:
   make -f boards/mps2-an500/mps2-an500.mk BUILD

4. Debug
   4.1 make DEBUG (start the GDB server)
   You should see:
   qemu-system-arm: -serial telnet:127.0.0.1:1124,server: info: QEMU waiting for connection on: disconnected:telnet:127.0.0.1:1124,server=on

   4.2 Run "telnet 127.0.0.1 1124"
   The QEMU gdbserver started with "-s" is NOT connectable with "target remote :1234" command in gdb client
   until above telnet step is finished. -- Be advised!

   4.3 Run GDB client
   arm-none-eabi-gdb
   target remote :1234
   file <path to the kernel.elf>
   (other debug commands)

